---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout title="Cookie Policy" description="Cookie policy for markspcparts.com">
  <Nav slot="nav" />

  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-16">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-slate-100 mb-2">Cookie Policy</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-steel mb-10">Last updated: October 13, 2026</p>

    <div class="prose prose-invert prose-sm max-w-none space-y-8 text-steel leading-relaxed">

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-200 mb-3">What are cookies</h2>
        <p>
          Cookies are small text files stored in your browser when you visit a website. They're used to remember preferences and track how people use a site.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-200 mb-3">How this site uses cookies</h2>
        <p>
          This site sets <strong class="text-slate-300">one category of cookies: analytics</strong>, enabled by default unless you opt out. There are no advertising cookies, no social media tracking pixels, and no third-party embeds that set cookies without your knowledge.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Separately from cookies, this site is served through <strong class="text-slate-300">Cloudflare</strong>, which runs its own network-level analytics beacon. It doesn't set a cookie and isn't affected by the Accept/Decline choice below — see the privacy policy for more on what it collects.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-200 mb-3">Analytics cookies (optional)</h2>
        <p>
          Unless you opt out, this site loads <strong class="text-slate-300">Google Analytics 4</strong> (GA4), which sets the following cookies:
        </p>
        <div class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto">
          <table class="w-full text-sm border-collapse">
            <thead>
              <tr class="border-b border-white/10">
                <th scope="col" class="text-left py-2 pr-4 text-slate-300 font-medium">Cookie</th>
                <th scope="col" class="text-left py-2 pr-4 text-slate-300 font-medium">Purpose</th>
                <th scope="col" class="text-left py-2 text-slate-300 font-medium">Duration</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody class="divide-y divide-white/5">
              <tr>
                <td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-xs text-accent-light">_ga</td>
                <td class="py-2 pr-4">Distinguishes unique visitors</td>
                <td class="py-2">2 years</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-xs text-accent-light">_ga_*</td>
                <td class="py-2 pr-4">Maintains session state for GA4</td>
                <td class="py-2">2 years</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-4">
          These cookies collect page views, session duration, approximate location, browser and device type. They do not collect personally identifiable information.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-200 mb-3">Your consent choice</h2>
        <p>
          When you first visit this site, a banner lets you know analytics is on and gives you the option to decline. Analytics loads as soon as you arrive; if you click Decline, no further analytics cookies are set. An anonymous cookieless ping may still reach Google — declining stops cookie-based tracking, not every network request.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Your choice is saved in your browser's <strong class="text-slate-300">local storage</strong> (not a cookie) so the banner doesn't appear on every page.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-200 mb-3">Withdrawing consent</h2>
        <p>
          Use the <strong class="text-slate-300">Cookie Settings</strong> link in the footer at any time to reopen the banner and change your choice.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Clearing local storage or site data also removes the saved choice, but it resets you to the <strong class="text-slate-300">default (granted)</strong> state on your next visit, not to declined — Cookie Settings is the reliable way to stay opted out.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-200 mb-3">More information</h2>
        <p>
          For details on how Google processes analytics data, see <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-accent-light hover:text-slate-300 underline underline-offset-2 transition-colors">Google's privacy policy</a>.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          For anything else, use the <a href="/contact/" class="text-accent-light hover:text-slate-300 underline underline-offset-2 transition-colors">contact page</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

    </div>
  </div>

  <Footer slot="footer" />
</Layout>
